# health/

Working example feature for ${PROJECT_NAME}. Real `GET /healthz` endpoint
that returns `{ status: "ok", uptime: <seconds> }`.

> **Intentionally tiny.** This feature exists to demonstrate the strict
> 4-subfolder rule, not to demo auth, DB access, or external calls. Do NOT
> expand it. If you need an auth or DB example, copy `_feature_template/`
> and build a separate feature.

## The strict 4-subfolder rule

Every feature folder has the same set of subfolders. Files live inside them,
never at the feature root.

| Subfolder | What lives here | File suffix |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [`routes/`](routes/) | Route registration | `*.routes.ts` |
| [`controllers/`](controllers/) | Request handlers — call the service, format the response | `*.controller.ts` |
| [`services/`](services/) | Business logic | `*.service.ts` |
| [`types/`](types/) | Request/response and domain types | `*.types.ts` |

## Endpoints

- `GET /healthz` → `200 { status: "ok", uptime: <seconds> }`

The route is mounted twice in [`${SRC_DIR}/app.ts`](../../../app.ts):

1. `/api/${API_VERSION}/health/` (versioned).
2. `/healthz` (unversioned — for orchestrator probes that don't know about your API version).

